  "materialInterpretation": {
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "material": "Matte aged dressed sandstone masonry, four ochre / grey-brown elongated stones around one rusty red sandstone square. Exact lithology and historical wall/floor use remain uncertain.",
    "observations": "The retained source, canonical RGB, decoded Mid256 and High512 visibly depict stone: coherent shallow bedding/fracture direction, granular aggregate, irregular fine pores and chipped weathered arrises. The red center remains the same kind of plausible mineral stone. It reads as physical masonry without relying on the material label. Fine detail is naturally organized, not a uniform grain overlay, tiled noise or enlarged native pixels."
  },
  "formsColourAndScale": {
    "verdict": "PASS representative native intent",
    "observations": "Five-stone pinwheel remains: left vertical ochre, top grey-brown horizontal, right vertical ochre, bottom horizontal ochre and central rusty red square. The distinctive larger native colour regions, relative proportions and orientation persist. Generated contours replace native pixel steps with natural stone arrises without adding small edge bricks, hardware, ornament or another perimeter frame. The replacement is somewhat brighter and warmer than the native; this is visible and consistent with representative similarity rather than pixel equality."
  },
